name\":\"• Layout, grouping, order and emphasis on every screen • All other colors: neutrals, text, backgrounds / surfaces (tints, gradients), overlays on photos, online / active, like, error / disabled • Type scale, spacing, radii, blur, elevation • All states: current tab, current profile tab, pressed, followed / liked, disabled • Headers, tab bar, tabs, story avatars, feed post, swipe card stack, action buttons, profile header, media grid, short-video overlay, sign-in sheet, drawer and menu rows • How photos are cropped and treated\",\"text\":\"• Layout, grouping, order and emphasis on every screen\\n• All other colors: neutrals, text, backgrounds / surfaces (tints, gradients), overlays on photos, online / active, like, error / disabled\\n• Type scale, spacing, radii, blur, elevation\\n• All states: current tab, current profile tab, pressed, followed / liked, disabled\\n• Headers, tab bar, tabs, story avatars, feed post, swipe card stack, action buttons, profile header, media grid, short-video overlay, sign-in sheet, drawer and menu rows\\n• How photos are cropped and treated\"},{\"id\":\"6:111\",\"name\":\"How it is evaluated\",\"text\":\"How it is evaluated\"},{\"id\":\"6:112\",\"name\":\"Your file is compared with this brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any original.\",\"text\":\"Your file is compared with this brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any original.\"},{\"id\":\"6:113\",\"name\":\"1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data & copy accuracy 3. Flow & prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality & consistency of your own system 6. Component reuse 7. State design (current tab, current profile tab, top card of the stack, sheet / drawer presentation)\",\"text\":\"1. Checklist coverage per frame\\n2. Data & copy accuracy\\n3. Flow & prototype completeness\\n4. Information hierarchy\\n5. Visual quality & consistency of your own system\\n6. Component reuse\\n7. State design (current tab, current profile tab, top card of the stack, sheet / drawer presentation)\"},{\"id\":\"6:114\",\"name\":\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 8 named frames, your components and the prototype.\",\"text\":\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 8 named frames, your components and the prototype.\"}]"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8909fe8-a8d8-4f9d-a111-170cbe1610c8","uuid":"9817802c-c827-49c2-ac13-f6fd30180951","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:59:27.318Z","tool_use_result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[{\"id\":\"6:4\",\"name\":\"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\",\"text\":\"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\"},{\"id\":\"6:5\",\"name\":\"Meet — dating and social app\",\"text\":\"Meet — dating and social app\"},{\"id\":\"6:6\",\"name\":\"Design Meet, a dating and social app: sign in, browse stories and posts on Explore, decide on suggested partners, visit a friend’s profile and watch a short, and manage your own profile from its menu. Canvas 393 × 852, iPhone, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\",\"text\":\"Design Meet, a dating and social app: sign in, browse stories and posts on Explore, decide on suggested partners, visit a friend’s profile and watch a short, and manage your own profile from its menu. Canvas 393 × 852, iPhone, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\"},{\"id\":\"6:8\",\"name\":\"How to work\",\"text\":\"How to work\"},{\"id\":\"6:9\",\"name\":\"1. Build exactly the 8 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in screen order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The two brand colors and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself (neutrals, text, backgrounds and surfaces including any tint or gradient, overlays on photos, online / active, like, error / disabled), plus type scale, spacing, radii, blur and elevation, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button and the platform shell (status bar, home indicator). Design all other states, the headers, the tab bar, the tabs, the sheet, the drawer and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the photos, logo and icons from 04 · Media. Each person always uses their own portrait. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\",\"text\":\"1. Build exactly the 8 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links.\\n2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in screen order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions.\\n3. The two brand colors and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself (neutrals, text, backgrounds and surfaces including any tint or gradient, overlays on photos, online / active, like, error / disabled), plus type scale, spacing, radii, blur and elevation, and apply them consistently.\\n4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button and the platform shell (status bar, home indicator). Design all other states, the headers, the tab bar, the tabs, the sheet, the drawer and every business component as reusable components in your file.\\n5. Use the photos, logo and icons from 04 · Media. Each person always uses their own portrait.\\n6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\"},{\"id\":\"6:11\",\"name\":\"Frames · goals · must include · links\",\"text\":\"Frames · goals · must include · links\"},{\"id\